## full commit message (remote)
test(custody): verify canonical request receipt binding

Close the I2A review findings on the canonical codec's assurance:

- A: the request receipt control now observes the digest the real core
  stores. Real requests go through Control::submit, Custody::serve,
  sequencing and execution in three custodies (one requiring recovery,
  so its retries run as real attempts); each retained receipt's digest,
  read through a cfg(test), read-only, per-instance accessor, must equal
  the digest of that request's version-1 frame, given literally by the
  independent derivation and re-derived from the frame with sha2. Pairs
  differing only in generation, sequence, operation or retry epoch are
  retained under different digests; duplicates and conflicts leave the
  retained digest unchanged.
- B: RecordIntent's documentation now states the digest's exact
  coverage: the frame header and payload, excluding the 32-byte digest
  trailer.

The accessor changes no core behaviour and offers no way to alter a
receipt. Codec, module documentation, the core regression target and the
version-1 wire format are unchanged.

